<title>GERMANY: Bewag H1 96/97 pretax profit flat.</title>
<headline>Bewag H1 96/97 pretax profit flat.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German state utility Berliner Kraft- und Licht AG (BEWAG) said on Thursday pretax profit in the first half of business year 1996/97 were little changed at 171.8 million marks ($101.7 million), down from 172.3 million marks in the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>First-half electricity revenue fell 1.2 percent to 6.4 billion marks, while heating revenue slipped 0.5 percent to 4.4 billion marks. Bewag is 50.8 percent owned by the Berlin government, which wants to privatise a 25.8 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150 ($ = 1.688 German Marks)</p>
